    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s May 11 slate, **Taylor Ward** stands out as the premier start with a 70.03 efficiency score. His matchup against Weathers (L) is bolstered by a significant +16% park factor adjustment, and hitting out of the leadoff spot provides the high-volume opportunity required to maximize our 5x5 production. Close behind is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.98), who remains a locked-in asset despite a neutral matchup against Suter (L), while the trio of **Luis Arraez** (66.78), **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65), and **Matt Chapman** (65.37) all benefit from a favorable encounter with Roki Sasaki. While Sasaki is an elite talent, his current 5.30 xERA allows our hitters to capture significant upside, particularly for **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Luis Arraez**, whose profiles thrive on high-contact environments that play well against power-pitching archetypes.\n\nThe primary lineup construction challenge today involves navigating several \"Lineup Pending\" designations. **Geraldo Perdomo** (57.57) holds the edge for our MI slot over utility depth options due to his projected #3 spot in the order, providing crucial stability in our counting categories. The most difficult personnel decision centered on **Daulton Varsho** (58.15); while he sits near the bottom of our active starters, his +2% adjustment for the slow delivery of Rasmussen (R) makes him a vital play for our scarce Stolen Base needs. **Drew Gilbert** (54.03) barely cleared the threshold for inclusion, but his presence is necessitated by the unfortunate IL designation of **Yainer Diaz** and the inactivity of **Lawrence Butler**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Tyler Freeman**, whose clubs are off today.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that five of our starters are currently confirmed against pending lineups. We are particularly monitoring the status of **Will Smith**; while his 49.41 score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Trevor McDonald (2.60 xERA), his projected #3 slot is vital for our RBI floor. Should any of the pending lineups shift these players down the order, we may see their efficiency scores drop toward the \"Marginal\" category. Consequently, we are prepared to monitor late-breaking news, though currently, our focus remains on leveraging the contact-heavy profiles of **Brendan Donovan** and **Jonathan Aranda** to sustain our AVG and R categories against mid-tier opposition.",
